# MATRU-NETRA Environment Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env and replace the placeholders with your actual credentials.
# Do NOT commit actual secrets or service-role keys to public version control.

# 1. Supabase Project URL (from Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co

# 2. Supabase Anonymous Public API Key (safe to use in browser client)
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-actual-anon-public-key

# Optional: how often (milliseconds) each device re-checks the shared database
# as a safety net in addition to live push updates. Default 30000 (30 seconds).
# VITE_SYNC_POLL_MS=30000

# Note:
# SHARED PATIENT DATABASE
# When VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are provided, MATRU-NETRA stores
# ALL patient records (mothers, visit reports, doctor reviews) in your Supabase database,
# so every verified ASHA worker and Doctor sees the same data from any device.
# Offline changes are kept on the device and uploaded automatically when internet returns.
#
# If they are NOT provided, the app runs in DEMO mode: records are saved only in this
# browser and are NOT shared between devices.
#
# These are build-time variables: set them in your host (Vercel / Netlify / GitHub Actions)
# before building, then redeploy. See supabase/SETUP_SHARED_DATABASE.md.
